{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018zYM4KVAaJN6WYUf2hQrLg","type":"tool_result","content":"55\tThe remaining items lift a setoid to a higher universe level, which Agda's\n56\tuniverse non-cumulativity makes necessary.\n57\t\n58\t+  `𝑙𝑖𝑓𝑡 ℓ`{.AgdaFunction} raises the level of the carrier and leaves the equality\n59\t   alone, relating two lifted elements exactly when the elements underneath them\n60\t   were related;\n61\t+  `liftFunc`{.AgdaFunction} is the setoid function into the lift;\n62\t+  `lift∼lower`{.AgdaFunction} and `lower∼lift`{.AgdaFunction} say that lifting\n63\t   and lowering are mutually inverse; both are proved by reflexivity alone, which\n64\t   is the point: the lifted equality *is* the original equality read through\n65\t   `lower`, so there is nothing to transport.\n66\t\n67\t```agda\n68\t𝑖𝑑 : {A : Setoid α ρᵃ} → A ⟶ A\n69\t𝑖𝑑 {A} = record { to = id ; cong = id }\n70\t\n71\topen _⟶_ renaming ( to to _⟨$⟩_ )\n72\t\n73\t_⊙_ :  {A : Setoid α ρᵃ}{B : Setoid β ρᵇ}{C : Setoid γ ρᶜ}\n74\t  →     B ⟶ C → A ⟶ B → A ⟶ C\n75\tf ⊙ g = record { to = (_⟨$⟩_ f) ∘ (_⟨$⟩_ g); cong = (cong f) ∘ (cong g) }\n76\t\n77\tmodule _ {𝑨 : Setoid α ρᵃ} where\n78\t  open Lift ; open Level ; open Setoid using (_≈_)\n79\t  open Setoid 𝑨 using ( sym ; trans ) renaming (Carrier to A ; _≈_ to _≈ₐ_ ; refl to reflₐ)\n80\t\n81\t  𝑙𝑖𝑓𝑡 : ∀ ℓ → Setoid (α ⊔ ℓ) ρᵃ\n82\t  𝑙𝑖𝑓𝑡 ℓ = record  { Carrier = Lift ℓ A\n83\t                 ; _≈_ = λ x y → (lower x) ≈ₐ (lower y)\n84\t                 ; isEquivalence = record { refl = reflₐ ; sym = sym ; trans = trans }\n85\t                 }\n86\t\n87\t  lift∼lower : (a : Lift β A) → (_≈_ (𝑙𝑖𝑓𝑡 β)) (lift (lower a)) a\n88\t  lift∼lower a = reflₐ\n89\t\n90\t  lower∼lift : ∀ a → (lower {α}{β}) (lift a) ≈ₐ a\n91\t  lower∼lift _ = reflₐ\n92\t\n93\t  liftFunc : {ℓ : Level} → 𝑨 ⟶ 𝑙𝑖𝑓𝑡 ℓ\n94\t  liftFunc = record { to = lift ; cong = id }\n95\t```\n96\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8955cd75-2e72-4386